From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: emuTOS-MCD <darekadumon@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 9 Aug 2026 09:53:58 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 016/185] segacd: PCM bell and keyclick, straight to the
 RF5C164

The PCM chip's registers and wave RAM are on the sub CPU's own bus,
odd bytes only, exactly like the internal backup RAM -- so no BIOS is
involved and the eviction costs nothing here. bell_hook and kcl_hook
now drive a decaying triangle one-shot on channel 0.

The sample terminates itself: its end marker loops onto another end
marker, so the channel falls silent on its own rather than depending
on the VBL countdown to switch it off. Without that a bell rung while
interrupts were not flowing would drone indefinitely; the countdown is
now only a backstop.

Verified as far as the emulators allow: wave RAM reads back byte-exact
through the bank window, but both cores stub the channel address
registers, so whether it is audible is untested. CONF_SEGACD_PCMTEST
is a boot-time diagnostic that reports the wave RAM check and the
channel address, for when a core or a real console can answer.
---
 bios/bios.c   | 47 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 bios/segacd.c | 94 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++
 bios/segacd.h |  5 +++
 bios/sound.c  |  9 +++++
 4 files changed, 155 insertions(+)

